{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-009", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India specialty fibres rise 2-3%: Is the premium gap widening?", "content": "India's specialty cellulosic fibre complex saw all eight specialty SKUs reprice on October 1 during September 28–October 2, then hold levels through Friday.\nEcovero rose 2.94–3.23 per cent, Liva Eco 2.14–2.36 per cent and Modal 2.22–2.41 per cent.\nMost standard benchmarks in China, India and Pakistan were flat, widening selected specialty-to-standard fibre spreads by 5–10 per cent.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-specialty-fibres-rise-2-3-is-the-premium-gap-widening--314017-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-010", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Vietnam posts $1.27 bn trade surplus in September 2026", "content": "Vietnam recorded a $1.27 billion merchandise trade surplus in September, ending nine straight months of deficit, the National Statistics Office said.\nTrade turnover reached $117.69 billion in the month, up 7.3 per cent month-on-month and 42.4 per cent year-on-year.\nFirst-nine-month trade still showed a $19.42 billion deficit as imports rose faster than exports.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-posts-1-27-bn-trade-surplus-in-september-2026-314008-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-011", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India's economy to grow 7.1% in FY27: World Bank", "content": "India’s economy is projected to grow 7.1 per cent in FY27, supported by domestic demand and exports, the World Bank said. \nMedium-term prospects remained strong despite risks from oil prices, El Niño and market corrections.\nPrivate AI investment rose to $4.1 billion in 2025, while the bank urged stronger infrastructure, wider access and workforce development to ensure broadly shared AI benefits. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-economy-to-grow-7-1-in-fy27-world-bank-314003-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-012", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indian cabinet approves $1.04 bn SME Growth Fund", "content": "India’s Cabinet has approved a ₹10,000 crore (~$1.04 billion) government commitment to set up the SME Growth Fund for direct equity investments in small and medium enterprises.\nThe fund targets a gap in long-term growth capital, with majority allocation for manufacturing-focused SMEs.\nIt will also consider SMEs in industrial clusters in Tier-II and Tier-III cities.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/indian-cabinet-approves-1-04-bn-sme-growth-fund-314013-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-013", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": -0.17, "keywords": ["improve", "weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cotton yarn prices dip in south India, but optimism persists", "content": "South Indian cotton yarn prices remained under pressure as weak downstream demand and lower ICE cotton pushed Mumbai and Tiruppur lower.\nMumbai yarn fell ₹3–7 (~$0.03–0.07) per kg and Tiruppur dropped ₹2–3 per kg as mills adjusted rates; traders saw scope for buying to improve after inventories reduced.\nGujarat cotton recovered ₹500 per candy despite rising new-season arrivals and high-moisture Kapas.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/cotton-yarn-prices-dip-in-south-india-but-optimism-persists-314004-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-014", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["growth", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Japan's Sanyo Shokai maintains FY27 profit plan after H1 loss", "content": "Japan's Sanyo Shokai maintained its FY27 plan despite a wider H1 loss, targeting ¥60 billion (~$379.79 million sales). \nH1 net sales fell 4 per cent YoY to ¥25.95 billion (~$164.26 million); operating loss widened and gross margin slipped to 60.4 per cent. \nRecovery rests on 11 per cent September retail sales growth, tighter markdowns, full-price selling and e-commerce expansion.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/japan-s-sanyo-shokai-maintains-fy27-profit-plan-after-h1-loss-314010-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-015", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["order_visibility", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "$5,059 freight gap meets tariffs: What really decides Asian sourcing?", "content": "Asian apparel sourcing is being reshaped by a $5,059 per FEU gap between routes to the US West Coast and North Europe, enough to erase narrow FOB advantages.\nJanuary-July 2026 data show China, India and Vietnam fared better in Europe, while Cambodia grew 10.9 per cent in the US despite higher freight.\nTariffs, EU preferences, product mix, lead times and Suez risk now decide competitiveness.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/-5-059-freight-gap-meets-tariffs-what-really-decides-asian-sourcing--314002-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-06-016", "date": "2026-10-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cambodia’s $212 wage: Who wins, who loses and fight behind the figure", "content": "Cambodia has set a $212 monthly minimum wage for garment, textile, footwear and travel-goods workers from January 1, 2027, up $2 from $210.\nWorkers had sought $225 after unions earlier demanded $250.66; employers wanted to retain $210 with a temporary $2.50 allowance.\nThe sector employs nearly one million workers and exported $11.76 billion in the first eight months of 2026, up 7.2 per cent.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/cambodia-s-212-wage-who-wins-who-loses-and-fight-behind-the-figure-313948-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
